From: Linux psX contributors
Subject: [PATCH] radv: expose the existing metadata fill offset bound to NIR

radv_compute_fill_memory asserts size <= UINT32_MAX and passes max_offset
as size minus bytes_per_invocation. Preserve that invariant in the shader.
The clamp is a no-op for every valid caller input, including short fills.

Without an explicit bound, ACO conservatively permits offset+store_width
to overflow 32 bits. On GFX7/8 it then combines the uniform address and
divergent offset into a VGPR address, selecting FLAT instead of the existing
MUBUF path. Do not weaken ACO's overflow check; expose the caller's range.

A device-hidden, submission-free Bonaire comparator compiled the original
meta_fill_memory_16B to flat_store_dwordx4. Verify the new lowered output
separately. This is a candidate for the shared metadata-fill failure path;
it does not prove defective FLAT execution on Liverpool or a hardware fix.
The failed cube also showed that the HTILE-disable workaround is insufficient.

License: MIT; existing per-file notices remain unchanged.

---
--- a/src/amd/vulkan/nir/radv_meta_nir.c
+++ b/src/amd/vulkan/nir/radv_meta_nir.c
@@ -146,6 +146,12 @@
    nir_def *pconst = nir_load_push_constant(&b, 4, 32, nir_imm_int(&b, 0), .range = 16);
    nir_def *buffer_addr = nir_pack_64_2x32(&b, nir_channels(&b, pconst, 0b0011));
    nir_def *max_offset = nir_channel(&b, pconst, 2);
+   /* The caller bounds size to UINT32_MAX and subtracts the store width.
+    * Preserve that range in NIR so GFX7/8 can use a MUBUF descriptor
+    * without a possible 32-bit offset overflow forcing FLAT.
+    */
+   max_offset = nir_umin(&b, max_offset,
+                         nir_imm_int(&b, UINT32_MAX - bytes_per_invocation));
    nir_def *data = nir_swizzle(&b, nir_channel(&b, pconst, 3), (unsigned[]){0, 0, 0, 0}, bytes_per_invocation / 4);
 
    nir_def *global_id =
